\ a ring filled between two radii about a centre, 48 pairs of triangles round it, its middle left clear
: fill-ring ( cx cy inner outer colour -- )
	| cx cy inner outer colour |
	0 48 1 do k
		k 48 / TAU * to from
		k 1+ 48 / TAU * to onto
		cx from sin inner * + cy from cos inner * -
		cx from sin outer * + cy from cos outer * -
		cx onto sin outer * + cy onto cos outer * - colour fill-face
		cx from sin inner * + cy from cos inner * -
		cx onto sin outer * + cy onto cos outer * -
		cx onto sin inner * + cy onto cos inner * - colour fill-face
	loop ;

\ the control column and its spade grip, a ring with the gun button on it, standing over the directional gyro: the ring moves right and left with the roll and toward the pilot when pulled back; the button red while firing
: draw-column ( -- )
	320 controls@roll 14 * + to grip-x
	lower-row controls@pitch 10 * + to grip-y
	grip-y 42 + to shaft-top
	-5 6 1 do k
		320 k + 480 grip-x k + shaft-top grip-colour draw-segment
	loop
	314 480 grip-x 6 - shaft-top grip-edge-colour draw-segment
	326 480 grip-x 6 + shaft-top grip-edge-colour draw-segment
	grip-x grip-y 30 42 grip-colour fill-ring
	grip-x grip-y 42 grip-edge-colour draw-circle
	grip-x grip-y 30 grip-edge-colour draw-circle
	grip-x 25 - grip-y 25 - 7 :firing game@ if 0xff4030 else brass-colour then fill-disc ;

\ the GM2's ring, 59 mils in radius, and the range at which the range bars are set, 300 yards
0.059 constant sight-ring-angle
274 constant sight-range
\ the wingspan the range bars are set for, the raid's bomber's
variable sight-span
20.08 to sight-span

