\ === the Hurricane's cockpit ===

\ The Hurricane Mk I's cockpit, laid out from the Smithsonian's Mk IIC
\ (NASM A19700066000, photographed from the seat) and the labelled panel of
\ the "Battle of Britain - Hurricane" simulation's manual. The same
\ blind-flying panel stands in the middle, its rows closer together, under
\ the reflector sight's pedestal and its padded crash pad. Three boards
\ stand side by side across the panel, as in photographs of the cockpit:
\ the left board, the blind-flying panel and the right board, sharing one
\ top and one foot, laid out after a labelled picture of a flight
\ simulator's Hurricane I cockpit. The left board, top to bottom: the
\ indicator lamps' switches and the undercarriage indicator, its P and S
\ windows red for locked up and green for locked down; the buzzer's
\ warning plate and the lamps' plate; the oxygen regulator's nameplate,
\ its delivery and supply dials and its brass valve handle; the emergency
\ boost knob, a red ring round a yellow face, and the clock; along the
\ foot the two engine starting buttons, the magneto switches' plate and
\ three bat-handled toggle switches under their plate. The right board:
\ the revolution counter, one hand over hundreds, at the top left and the
\ gunsight's switch at the top right; the boost gauge in its red rim under
\ the counter and the fuel gauge's selector for the port, centre and
\ starboard tanks under the switch; the oil pressure's orange strip gauge
\ and the fuel pressure's red one side by side under the boost gauge, the
\ fuel gauge beside them; the oil and radiator temperatures along the
\ foot, their rims orange and brass, the starting magneto's switch and the
\ primer's knob at the right. The undercarriage indicator and the
\ revolution counter stand on the coaming in the aircraft; they are on the
\ boards here, the coaming above them too shallow for their dials. The
\ picture shows no brake pressure gauge, and none is drawn. The lamp
\ switches, the supply dial, the magnetos, the toggle switches, the sight
\ and starting magneto switches and the primer are drawn and do nothing.
\ On the right wall the one
\ lever that works the wheels and the flaps, in its gate, the selector
\ returned to neutral after each use, the flaps' placard and their
\ indicator. On the left wall the throttle quadrant, the elevator trim's
\ wooden handwheel edge-on with the pointer plate beside it that reads the
\ tab between NOSE DOWN and NOSE UP, and above them the rudder bias knob,
\ its eight lobes turning with the setting. The panel's top arched as
\ the Spitfire's, the side boards running to the screen's bottom; below
\ the blind panel the compass bowl under the column's shaft and the
\ Spitfire's frame pedals. In the windscreen, faint, the frame of the
\ armoured panel. The clock runs from twelve with the flight's time. The
\ fuel cock turns between the main tanks and the reserve on the R key, its
\ position shown by the fuel gauge's selector pointer, and the gauge reads
\ the tanks the engine draws from.

\ the Hurricane's rows of blind-flying dials, the column's ring and the boards' top; the foot of the panel's old sections, which the tubes below run from, and the boards' shared foot
panel-top 70 + constant hurricane-upper-row
panel-top 148 + constant hurricane-lower-row
panel-top 30 + constant blind-panel-top
panel-top 186 + constant panel-foot
panel-top 190 + constant board-foot

\ a board of the panel from its left edge to its right, from the blind-flying panel's top to the shared foot
: draw-board ( left right colour -- )
	| left right colour |
	left blind-panel-top right left - board-foot blind-panel-top - colour fill-span
	left blind-panel-top right left - board-foot blind-panel-top - edge-colour outline ;

\ a side board from its left edge to its right, from a row under the arch to the screen's bottom
